  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), F/A-18 stick grip alone (no base) seen from behind (pilot side) and above: head with red button, castle hat, trim hat and small hat facing the viewer; post hat on the left of the grip; trigger and pinky paddle peeking out at the right (front)",
  "mappingSource": "WinWing \"J2-ORION JOYSTICK BASE-MANUAL EN V1.0\" section 2.2 Grip Function drawing, page 2 (https://en.winwing.cn/static/file/J2-ORION%20JOYSTICK%20BASE-MANUAL%20EN%20V%201.0.pdf): 7 = round button top-left, 2-6 = castle hat in the middle of the head, 1 = 8-way trim hat (NOSE UP/DOWN, L/R WD), 8/18-21 = small hat below the castle, 11-15 = post hat on the left side of the grip, 9/10 = trigger, 16 = side button, 17 = pinky paddle; matches the catalog numbers (the catalog cites the J1/J2 base manuals). The part names DMS/CMS are the catalog's inference.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "note": "The side button 16 (catalog stick.pinky.button) is on the right side of the grip and not visible here (gallery-4 shows it). Roll/pitch come from the base; the gimbal marker sits at the grip's threaded base joint. JOY_Z twist exists only with the optional Z-axis kit (F18 HOTAS install guide), the marker sits on the handle.",
